  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145710",
      "title": "Introducing \"getServerSideProps\" for Server-side Rendering (SSR)",
      "lectureOrder": 281,
      "videoOrder": 262,
      "sourceHash": "c417301ebd0e408854d75da7ebe27a41236c0d87d2fc29429d5f37df668819f0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 3.77,
          "en": "So now we had a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.77,
          "end": 7.64,
          "en": "getStaticProps and getStaticPaths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.64,
          "end": 10.11,
          "en": "And these two are working together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.11,
          "end": 12.01,
          "en": "You don't always need both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.01,
          "end": 15.87,
          "en": "In the case of index.js, we only needed getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.87,
          "end": 19.06,
          "en": "But for dynamic pages, that should be pre-generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.06,
          "end": 20.93,
          "en": "you do need both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.93,
          "end": 24.97,
          "en": "Now you might recall that earlier in this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.97,
          "end": 27.61,
          "en": "at the beginning of this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.61,
          "end": 29.29,
          "en": "I showed you this slide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.29,
          "end": 34.28,
          "en": "and I referred to two forms of pre-rendering:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.28,
          "end": 38.12,
          "en": "static generation and server-side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.12,
          "end": 41.17,
          "en": "Now what we had a look at thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.17,
          "end": 43.55,
          "en": "that's static generation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.55,
          "end": 47.57,
          "en": "because we statically pre-generate pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.57,
          "end": 49.77,
          "en": "Even though it's not fully static",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.77,
          "end": 52.41,
          "en": "because of incremental static generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.41,
          "end": 53.92,
          "en": "which I also explained,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.92,
          "end": 57.343,
          "en": "but generally pages are pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.24,
          "end": 60.08,
          "en": "And that is really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.08,
          "end": 64.99,
          "en": "Inside of getStaticProps and also inside of getStaticPaths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.99,
          "end": 69.09,
          "en": "we don't have access to the actual request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.09,
          "end": 70.8,
          "en": "which is incoming.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.8,
          "end": 73.82,
          "en": "Because these functions are not called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.82,
          "end": 77.72,
          "en": "for the actual request, at least not only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.72,
          "end": 79.94,
          "en": "With incremental static generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.94,
          "end": 83.37,
          "en": "they are also called for incoming requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.37,
          "end": 87.5,
          "en": "at least sometimes if they need to be re-validated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.5,
          "end": 92.4,
          "en": "but they are generally called when your project is built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.4,
          "end": 94.95,
          "en": "So inside of getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.95,
          "end": 99.95,
          "en": "you don't have access to the actual incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.07,
          "end": 103.94,
          "en": "Now, very often, you also don't need access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.94,
          "end": 107.57,
          "en": "For example, here in the examples I showed you thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.57,
          "end": 110.56,
          "en": "we don't need access to the actual request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.56,
          "end": 112.50999999999999,
          "en": "which is reaching the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.50999999999999,
          "end": 115.67,
          "en": "But sometimes static generation is not enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.67,
          "end": 119.93,
          "en": "and instead, you need real server-side rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.93,
          "end": 124.93,
          "en": "which means that you do need to pre-render a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125,
          "end": 127.57,
          "en": "for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.57,
          "end": 129.71,
          "en": "So not at most every second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.71,
          "end": 132.76,
          "en": "but really for every incoming request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.76,
          "end": 137.76,
          "en": "and/or you need access to the concrete request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.84,
          "end": 139.64,
          "en": "that is reaching the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.64,
          "end": 143.22,
          "en": "Because, for example, you need to extract cookies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.22,
          "end": 146.7,
          "en": "And that is something we're also going to see later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 149.93,
          "en": "in the course when we talk about authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.93,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "but I already want to introduce you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 156.19,
          "en": "to real server-side rendering here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.19,
          "end": 158.05,
          "en": "The idea is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.05,
          "end": 159.44,
          "en": "NextJS also supports this run real server-side code use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.44,
          "end": 164.44,
          "en": "NextJS also supports this run real server-side code use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.73,
          "end": 167.55,
          "en": "which means it gives you a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.55,
          "end": 171.07,
          "en": "which you can add to your page component files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.07,
          "end": 172.828,
          "en": "which is then really executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.828,
          "end": 177.74,
          "en": "whenever a request for this page reaches the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.74,
          "end": 181.28,
          "en": "So that's then not pre-generated in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.28,
          "end": 184.66,
          "en": "during build time or every couple of seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.66,
          "end": 188.86,
          "en": "but it's really code that runs on the server only,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.86,
          "end": 191.44,
          "en": "so only after you deployed it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.44,
          "end": 196.44,
          "en": "and which is then re-executed for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.06,
          "end": 200.426,
          "en": "And that code is added to a function called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.426,
          "end": 202.593,
          "en": "getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 207.63,
          "en": "Just like getStaticProps, it's a async function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.63,
          "end": 210.61,
          "en": "It needs to be called exactly like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.61,
          "end": 212.65,
          "en": "and it needs to be exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.65,
          "end": 216.29,
          "en": "And you can only add it to your page component files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.29,
          "end": 218.6,
          "en": "But then if you do have such a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.6,
          "end": 220.44,
          "en": "in a page component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.44,
          "end": 224.853,
          "en": "NextJS will execute that function and it will execute it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.853,
          "end": 228.54,
          "en": "whenever a request for this page is made.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.54,
          "end": 233.11599999999999,
          "en": "And therefore, you should only use either getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.11599999999999,
          "end": 234.91,
          "en": "what we saw thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.91,
          "end": 239.73,
          "en": "or getServerSideProps because they kind of clash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.73,
          "end": 242.11,
          "en": "They fulfill the same purpose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.11,
          "end": 244.44,
          "en": "They get props for the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.44,
          "end": 248.72,
          "en": "so that NextJS is then able to render that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.72,
          "end": 251.863,
          "en": "but they run at different points of time.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
